                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1][b]I have mixed opinions about this one[/b][/h1]\nI really want to enjoy this game, but there are too many aspects that it falls short in. I'm a fan of the Killing Floor series and I can tell that the developer of this game is too based on his display of achievements in it. This game is fairly similar to it and it almost seems that the dev had a bit of influence from it. The main problem that I have, however is that the game says how it has a ton of replayablity. I do not agree with this because it feels like it's the same thing over and over again. Levelling up in this game grants you new special characters to summon, but it also gives you a skin for the only weapon.\n\n[b] Short Version [/b]\nThe weapon that you have to use feels like you're throwing rocks at most of enemies. \nThe reload speed is extremely slow and the normal walk speed for your character is slower than almost every single enemy. \nThe missile shooting enemies are able to shoot their missiles through the world, so you could be hit by a missile with little to no chance to move because it goes through the house you're standing in or through the large object next to you obstructing your vision.\n\n[b] Long Version [/b]\nThe main problems I have is with the progression and gunplay. The game does not make me feel like I am progressing or becoming stronger at all. After about an hour of gameplay, I'm only level 4 and have the giant turd ally unlocked and a few weapon skins. The items that you can pick up are most of the time useless, especially the defender cat characters. Half of the time, they get lost or disappear. If you're lucky enough to keep yours, then it shoots once every 5 seconds or so. This wouldn't be so bad, if most of the enemies didn't take 9 bullets to kill. Also, the reload speed of the gun takes about 5 seconds and has a magazine size of 25. When you have to use half of your mag to kill most of the enemies, and have to almost constantly sprint to avoid being hit, I feel like I'm reloading almost as much as I'm shooting. The map design on almost every level is pretty neat and enjoyable, except for \"Ice Level 3\" (The shield was gone, but it kept blocking my shots on basic enemies that kept spawning and innevitably caused my death), but some of the main enemies just feel like bullet sponges and it spawns too many of them to deal with most of the time. The design and models of the bosses look great and are creative, but quite a few of the bosses feel the exact same. Most of them just sprint really fast towards you and spawn some sort of common enemy found in that level type.\n\n[b]In Conclusion[/b]\nAs I said before, I really enjoy this type of game, however I feel like I'm doing the exact same thing over and over again with little to no meaningful progression. I just unlock enemy types and weapon skins for levelling up with the occasional ally thrown in every few levels. I feel like this could be a great game because it is very creative and has quite a cool concept, but it lacks in the gameplay and progression. I cannot recommend this game in it's current state, and especially not for $8.\n\n[b]Quick Edit[/b]\nI will be checking in on this title as it continues to be updated because I really want this game to be good. I enjoy the creepiness and the concept of the game is very interesting. I also like how the developer is active in his threads and reads reviews to get community input for future potential updates. I hope that this game gets more traction and succeeds because I really enjoy the good things about it.",
